; dot-forms.md §5 step 3: a bare symbol in selector position is an ordinary
; variable, so `(p k)` reads the LOCAL `k` as a computed selector. `k` is an i32
; here, and a computed selector must evaluate to an interned symbol (ptr) --
; which is the refusal this fixture pins. The field reading is `(p 'k)`.
(import-use "stdio.h")
(defstruct Point x:i32 y:i32)
(defn main ():i32
  (let (p:ptr:Point (alloca Point) k:i32 1)
    (printf "%d\n" (p k))
    (return 0)))
